# Cloudflare redirects (https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/redirects/)
#
# Legacy-route redirects were dropped deliberately: the site is new enough that
# nothing external links to the retired paths (/metod/, /dokument/, /data/,
# /koalition/ and their EN counterparts), so they 404 rather than carrying a
# permanent redirect table forward. Note this only retires the bare index paths
# — /dokument/[slug]/ and /en/documents/[slug]/ are live pages, and the
# /dokument/ ↔ /documents/ pair must stay in SLUG_PAIRS for them to localize.
#
# @astrojs/sitemap emits sitemap-index.xml; alias the common /sitemap.xml guess
# to it. This one is not legacy routing — it is a convenience alias for a URL
# people and crawlers guess — so it stays.
/sitemap.xml  /sitemap-index.xml  301
